The error message I receive is:

Cannot analyze program with no method found to test

I suspect this is because I only run tests on a static method, even though several other test methods are present.  Can anyone guide me what other methods, besides those currently written, I can test?

A: You have not provided any testable state for the method under test. 

This is causing the problem because Pex does not know which instance of the ArrayList class to analyze and which inputs to use for the tests.

One way to fix it is to create a state object that represents a valid instance of the ArrayList class and pass it as an argument to the methods you want to test. This will make Pex aware of the class under test and the test inputs.

In your example, you can create an ArrayList instance as a state object and pass it to the other test methods you are writing.

Alternatively, you can use Pex to generate the inputs for you. There are several ways to instruct Pex how to generate the inputs it needs:

1) PexInlineAttribute: You can generate the inputs inline. This attribute tells Pex to automatically generate--------------------
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(New_Ret);
        }

